In article <1992Apr3.180552.14220@pellns.alleg.edu> test writes:
>Can anybody out there tell me ways to get rid of cursed objects?  I'm a  
>barbarian stuck with enough cursed armor to make my AC as poor as if I  
>weren't wearing any armor at all, and I have crystal plate mail that I want  
>to put on.

dipping an object in a fountain may remove the curse...if you see the water
in the fountain glow, the curse has been removed.  You can only do this for
one item at a time...dipping an item in holy water will remove curses....
if there is an alter to your diety nearby, kill a few levels until you see
a couple of four-leaf clovers appear at your feet...then pray.  If you are
not hungry, stunned, or any one of a number of other conditions, your god
may remove all of the curses at once...if you see it glow amber, the curse is
removed.

>Also, any spoilers on how to tell if an object is cursed or not would be  
>greatly appreciated.  The only way I know is by seeing if my pet will pick  
>it up or by using a scroll of identify, which is difficult to come across.
>

drop the item on any altar.  If it glows black it is cursed, amber means
blessed, and no aura means uncursed.  


